<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malaya</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malaya was the name for British territories on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>, comprising the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/straits-settlements">Straits Settlements</a> and the Malay states under British protection. It was valued for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s rapid conquest of Malaya and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> in 1941 to 1942 dealt a severe blow to the prestige of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>, and Malaya became independent in 1957.</p></div>
